================================================================================
2. .PHASE.LOCK STRUCTURE (FINALIZED)
================================================================================

Structure:
PHASE_LOCK_VERSION=1
LOCK_TIMESTAMP=<ISO 8601 UTC>
MANIFEST_HASH=<SHA256 of manifest.json>
CHAIN_HASH=<SHA256(MANIFEST_HASH + LOCK_TIMESTAMP)>
# This file is an immutable witness of deterministic build
# Modification indicates tampering

Immutability Enforcement:
- File permissions: 444 (read-only for owner, group, world)
- Set via CMake: file(CHMOD "${LOCK_PATH}" PERMISSIONS OWNER_READ GROUP_READ WORLD_READ)
- Modification blocked at filesystem level

Cryptographic Chain:
- MANIFEST_HASH: Direct hash of manifest.json content
- CHAIN_HASH: Hash of (MANIFEST_HASH concatenated with LOCK_TIMESTAMP)
- Prevents independent tampering of manifest or lock
- Any change to manifest breaks MANIFEST_HASH verification
- Any change to lock breaks CHAIN_HASH verification

File Location: ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/.phase.lock
Generated By: cmake/modules/PhaseLock.cmake (generate_phase_lock function)

================================================================================
3. CMAKE INTEGRATION
================================================================================

Location: /home/user/qlever/cmake/modules/PhaseLock.cmake

Functions Provided:
1. compute_digest(OUTPUT_VAR INPUT_PATH)
   - Computes SHA256 hash of file or directory tree
   - Recursive for directories (all files sorted by path)

2. compute_dependency_receipt(OUTPUT_VAR)
   - Generates JSON map of dependency name → hash
   - Covers: ICU, simdjson, FSST, Abseil

3. generate_manifest(MANIFEST_PATH ENGINE_VERSION BINARY_PATH SOURCE_DIRS GOLDEN_CORPUS_DIR)
   - Generates manifest.json with all cryptographic digests
   - Includes: version, timestamp, binary hash, logic hash, deps, corpus

4. generate_phase_lock(LOCK_PATH MANIFEST_PATH)
   - Generates .phase.lock witness file
   - Computes chain hash, sets read-only permissions

5. verify_phase_lock(LOCK_PATH MANIFEST_PATH RESULT_VAR)
   - Verifies manifest integrity against phase lock
   - Recomputes hashes, validates chain
   - Returns TRUE/FALSE, FATAL_ERROR on failure

6. add_phase_lock_target(TARGET_NAME ...)
   - CMake target for phase lock generation
   - Prevents rebuild tampering (verifies existing lock)
   - Integrates with build system

Usage Example:
```cmake
include(cmake/modules/PhaseLock.cmake)

add_phase_lock_target(phase_lock
    ENGINE_VERSION "1.0.0"
    BINARY_PATH "${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/ServerMain"
    SOURCE_DIRS "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/src/engine;${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/src/index"
    GOLDEN_CORPUS_DIR "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/test/golden"
)

add_dependencies(phase_lock ServerMain)
```

Build Enforcement:
- If .phase.lock already exists: verifies integrity before proceeding
- If verification fails: CMake FATAL_ERROR aborts build
- Prevents tampering between builds

Hash Algorithm Note:
- Current: SHA256 (available via CMake file() and OpenSSL)
- Specified: BLAKE3 (per EPIC 10.2 specification)
- Migration: Variable PHASE_LOCK_HASH_ALGO for future swap
- TODO: Vendor BLAKE3 or add as system dependency

================================================================================
4. VERIFICATION FUNCTION
================================================================================

Location: /home/user/qlever/src/util/PhaseLockVerifier.{h,cpp}

C++ API:

class PhaseLockVerifier {
public:
  // Load manifest from JSON file
  static std::optional<BuildManifest> loadManifest(
      const std::filesystem::path& manifestPath);

  // Load phase lock from witness file
  static std::optional<PhaseLock> loadPhaseLock(
      const std::filesystem::path& lockPath);

  // Verify phase lock integrity (returns true/false)
  static bool verify(
      const std::filesystem::path& lockPath,
      const std::filesystem::path& manifestPath);

  // Verify and throw exception on failure
  static void verifyOrThrow(
      const std::filesystem::path& lockPath,
      const std::filesystem::path& manifestPath);

  // Get build manifest info (for runtime introspection)
  static std::optional<BuildManifest> getBuildInfo(
      const std::filesystem::path& buildDir = ".");
};

Verification Algorithm:
1. Load .phase.lock, parse MANIFEST_HASH and CHAIN_HASH
2. Load manifest.json, parse all fields
3. Recompute SHA256 hash of manifest.json file
4. Compare recomputed hash with stored MANIFEST_HASH
   - If mismatch: return false, log INTEGRITY FAILURE
5. Recompute CHAIN_HASH = SHA256(MANIFEST_HASH + LOCK_TIMESTAMP)
6. Compare recomputed chain with stored CHAIN_HASH
   - If mismatch: return false, log INTEGRITY FAILURE
7. If all checks pass: return true

Runtime Integration Example:
```cpp
#include "util/PhaseLockVerifier.h"

int main() {
  try {
    PhaseLockVerifier::verifyOrThrow("build/.phase.lock", "build/manifest.json");
    LOG(INFO) << "Build integrity verified" << std::endl;
  } catch (const std::runtime_error& e) {
    LOG(ERROR) << "Build integrity compromised: " << e.what() << std::endl;
    return EXIT_FAILURE;
  }

  // ... start engine
}
```

Dependencies:
- OpenSSL (SHA256 via <openssl/sha.h>)
- std::filesystem (C++17)
- std::regex (for JSON parsing)

CMake Integration:
